Fly gives thrust in time with the flap; without a flap the force is
zero. Crow Glide is a slow sink (lift near weight, `|vy|` capped);
do not stall from cruise height — that is a dive. Fly cruise also
holds the wing in seeded pockets (`cruiseGlideChance`, staggered by
`flapPhaseOffset`) and look-banks (`cruiseBankLook`; Glide is milder).
